.TH "Docv::Term::Sequences" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Term::Sequences \- Escape sequences the viewer writes.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBmodule Docv::Term::Sequences\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Escape sequences the viewer writes.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.PP
\fBALT_SCREEN_OFF = "\ee[?1049l"\fR
.PP
\fBALT_SCREEN_ON = "\ee[?1049h"\fR
.PP
\fBCLIPBOARD = "\ee]52;c;"\fR
.TP 4
\fBCLIPBOARD_CLEAR = "\ee]52;c;!\ee\e\e"\fR
OSC 52 clipboard write: the start before the base64 text. An invalid
payload first clears the clipboard in terminals that append writes
(kitty).
.TP 4
\fBCOLORS_QUERY\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
COLORS_QUERY = "\ee]21;foreground=?;background=?;#{(0..15).join(\(aq;\(aq) do |index| "#{index}=?" end}\ee\e\e"
.EE
.RE
.PP
OSC 21 query of the terminal theme: foreground, background and the 16
ANSI colors.
.RE
.PP
\fBCURSOR_HIDE = "\ee[?25l"\fR
.PP
\fBCURSOR_SHOW = "\ee[?25h"\fR
.TP 4
\fBHYPERLINK = "\ee]8;;"\fR
OSC 8 hyperlink: the start before the URI and the string terminator
after it; an empty URI ends the link.
.PP
\fBKEYBOARD_POP = "\ee[<u"\fR
.TP 4
\fBKEYBOARD_PUSH = "\ee[>31u"\fR
Kitty keyboard: push all five enhancements, pop on exit.
.PP
\fBMOUSE_OFF = "\ee[?1003;1006;1016l"\fR
.TP 4
\fBMOUSE_ON = "\ee[?1003;1006;1016h"\fR
Any\-event tracking with SGR\-pixel coordinates (SGR cells as fallback).
.PP
\fBNOTIFY_OFF = "\ee[?2048l\ee[?1004l\ee[?2033l\ee[?2031l"\fR
.TP 4
\fBNOTIFY_ON = "\ee[?2048h\ee[?1004h\ee[?2033h\ee[?2031h"\fR
In\-band resize, focus, visibility and color scheme notifications.
.TP 4
\fBPOINTER = "\ee]22;"\fR
OSC 22 pointer shape: the start before a CSS cursor name and the
string terminator after it; an empty name resets the shape.
.TP 4
\fBQUERIES = "\ee[?1016$p\ee[16t\ee[?u\ee[?998n\ee[?996n"\fR
Queries: pixel mouse mode, cell size, keyboard flags, visibility, scheme.
.PP
\fBRESET = "\ee[0m"\fR
.PP
\fBSYNC_BEGIN = "\ee[?2026h"\fR
.PP
\fBSYNC_END = "\ee[?2026l"\fR
.PP
\fBTERMINATOR = "\ee\e\e"\fR
